=== FS-66 phase 1a: the checkpoint/resume discipline, exercised on purpose ===
The tool is tools/fs66_minimise.py -- the same code the production run uses. The mode here is edge
deletion, only because its probes cost 120,000-150,000 conflicts each and the run therefore lasts long
enough to interrupt; the production vertex run finishes in 15.7 s (see minimise-p11-l2.log).
THE AUDIT QUESTION, answered BEFORE launching: if this process dies right now, what does the relaunch redo?
  data/fs66/ckpt/resume-exercise.current.json is rewritten atomically (temp file, fsync, rename) after
  EVERY wave, and carries the vertex list, the edge list, the pin, the accepted deletions and the set of
  candidates already probed against THIS graph. So the relaunch redoes at most the one wave in flight.
  resume: python3 tools/fs66_minimise.py --resume data/fs66/ckpt/resume-exercise.current.json

